## 10. Greedy marginal allocation and the Readiness Frontier

**Objective.** Minimise expected material-related downtime, weighted by the archetype's AOG cost and the rectification window, for a given spares capital.

**Algorithm.** The analytic model (`gnm.optim.model`) gives expected downtime per part from a hub + outstation (METRIC-lite) model. When AUH is out of stock, a need waits for own supply or the v2 AOG route, whichever comes first; downtime counts only when late and includes fitting/RTS; cost = hours × hourly rate + events × fixed cost + route fees (V2-OPT-1). Starting from P2 within guardrails, the greedy repeatedly adds the (PN, station) unit with the largest reduction in weighted downtime per AED of capital. Greedy is optimal only for separable, convex objectives at its breakpoints; hub-station coupling and per-aircraft merging break separability, so it is a heuristic here. Check: {{RESULT:optim.greedy_gap_small_case_pct}}.

**Guardrails, stated before computing** (V2-OPT-2). G1: at each stocking point the total spares may not exceed the 99.5% fill quantile of that point's own pipeline. G2: a station with at most 6 requests a year for the part holds at most 1 unit. Above those levels the tail is cheaper to cover with the AOG routes than with idle stock. They cost {{RESULT:frontier.guard_cost}} of material AOG a year at P2's capital (selection seeds).

**Candidates and the rule.** {{RESULT:frontier.n_candidates}} candidates were frozen (candidates.json {{RESULT:freeze.candidates_sha}}): P0, P1 and P2; 16 re-optimised budget points; P2 within guardrails; two "P2 + greedy additions" points (I110, I125); a reposition-only point; a TAT-cut lever and a budget + TAT combination. All were run on the selection seeds, and the recommendation rule was applied there, before the holdout:

> {{RESULT:frontier.recommendation_rule}}

With P2's realised {{RESULT:frontier.aed_per_aog_hour}} per downtime hour (the fixed cost per event spread over its hours, V2-OPT-3), h* = {{RESULT:frontier.h_star}} hours per AED 1M at {{RESULT:frontier.carrying_pct}} carrying cost. The rule picked **I125** on the selection seeds: {{RESULT:frontier.sel.I125_aog}} against {{RESULT:frontier.sel.P2_aog}} for P2, paired {{RESULT:frontier.sel.I125_vs_P2}}, net {{RESULT:frontier.sel.I125_net}} a year. The pick is {{RESULT:fo.carrying_stable}}, but moves to {{RESULT:fo.rule_shift}}.

**Holdout.** I125 costs {{RESULT:fo.extra_capital}} more than P2 for {{RESULT:fo.aog_reduction}} {{RESULT:fo.aog_reduction_ci}} less material AOG a year and {{RESULT:fo.total_cost_saving}} lower total annual cost. At P2's own capital the best re-optimised allocation (B100) is {{RESULT:frontier.B100_vs_P2}} vs P2: P2 is already near the frontier. Model vs simulation: {{RESULT:frontier.model_vs_sim}}.

